I'm happy that I can put a smile on  someone's face when they're eating a  pastry I created hi I'm June  today I'm making chiffon cake I am a  pastry chef had proof bakery in Los  Angeles chiffon cake is a very classic  light cake it's like angel food cake  virgin wash so it's very light very nice  to eat especially on a summer time I  moved from the Philippines to the US  here in Los Angeles when I was 20 and I  instantly went to the culinary school  and the rest is history it's special  because it's the first cake I learned  from my mother and I was very excited  about it and very technique-driven cake  and I'm happy that I learned it from her  I make this cake usually where  somebody's birthday at home or a cousin  so everybody likes this cake making  meringue can be very difficult if we  don't understand the technicality of it  we wanted to make sure that after we  whip it we have a nice glossy texture of  fine texture in it and there's no pieces  of sugar when you're incorporating the  base and the meringue that you made we  want to do two folding techniques so  you're not popping all the air pockets  that you create it into the meringue  because that's what makes the cake rises  as you bake we don't use eggs in our  buttercream we use butter evaporated  milk and sugar because eggs are pretty  pricey back in Manila where I grew up  only use it in the cakes that we bake  and then the buttercream is just use  butter sugar and milk I knew I was gay  when I was younger I knew it right away  that was different I was different from  the other boys that I see the  neighborhood the different from the boys  that I see in school but I didn't come  out till I was 22 I was already here in  Los Angeles with my family and that's  when I decided to come out I pretty much  grew up in church there was a huge  battle between what I'm feeling and who  I am and my religious background so it  was hard for me to accept who I really  am in the beginning when I started  working in the kitchens it was hard you  know I see my being gay was a downfall  as a weakness but then I realized no  it's not it's my power in the end you  would earn  spec's because she would show what you  can do it would see what you can do and  you just have to pretty much prove  yourself every day and not stop but I  tell most of my co-workers this not to  stop learning and to always be accepting  of criticisms it's pretty much how you  will learn and grow is accepting that  and learning from that and I still  learned until now even though I've been  in the business for a while every time I  come to work I still learn something new  for young people or any person that's  gay and wanted to be a chef I mean just  be yourself you don't have to hide  anything be humble and just be kind  if anybody listening to this and you're  struggling and coming out to anybody to  your parents or to your loved ones to  your to your friends take your time it  will happen when you're ready do not  force yourself to come out I know it's  hard  trust your feeling there are better  things after when you come out oh oh yes  [Music]
 

